WEBVTT

1
00:00:09.318 --> 00:00:12.280
only time I feel alive is when I'm painting."

2
00:00:13.041 --> 00:00:16.764
These words were written by one of the greatest painters, Vincent van Gogh.

3
00:00:17.524 --> 00:00:22.608
While van Gogh's life was full of disappointments and tragedy, he was able to overcome these in his

4
00:00:22.768 --> 00:00:27.032
art. He produced some of the most important masterpieces of all time.

5
00:00:27.892 --> 00:00:31.936
In his art, van Gogh created his own world of light, hope, and happiness.

6
00:00:33.488 --> 00:00:36.689
Vincent van Gogh was born in Holland in 1853.

7
00:00:37.510 --> 00:00:41.431
He had a happy childhood and grew up in a small village called Groot-Zundert.

8
00:00:42.332 --> 00:00:47.414
Young Vincent enjoyed playing alone in the nearby fields and often made sketches of the plants he found.

9
00:00:48.274 --> 00:00:52.456
He liked to draw at an early age, but he didn't become an artist until later in life.

10
00:00:53.837 --> 00:00:57.638
Van Gogh was first an art dealer and later a church minister like his father.

11
00:00:58.518 --> 00:01:01.940
He worked as an art dealer, but he was not very good at serving the public.

12
00:01:02.836 --> 00:01:07.160
He was often rude to customers, and he disliked the idea of art being bought and sold.

13
00:01:08.040 --> 00:01:14.906
After studying to be a minister, in 1879 van Gogh moved to Borinage, Belgium, a village of coal

14
00:01:14.946 --> 00:01:19.149
miners. It was in Borinage that van Gogh started to paint.

15
00:01:19.950 --> 00:01:22.012
The Potato Eaters is dark and gloomy.

16
00:01:22.792 --> 00:01:26.495
Its colors communicate the hard life that the miners and their families suffered.

17
00:01:27.376 --> 00:01:29.058
Vincent painted life as he saw it.

18
00:01:29.798 --> 00:01:31.720
He felt great kindness for the miners.

19
00:01:32.500 --> 00:01:37.123
However, even though he often gave away his clothes and furniture, he was not a good minister.

20
00:01:38.543 --> 00:01:41.885
Van Gogh left for Paris, the center of art and culture in Europe.

21
00:01:42.786 --> 00:01:46.988
Once Vincent moved to Paris, his palette and his feelings about life changed.

22
00:01:47.748 --> 00:01:50.030
He had renewed energy and enthusiasm.

23
00:01:50.790 --> 00:01:56.933
Instead of the old clothes he wore in Borinage, he wore a colorful scarf, a fashionable hat, and

24
00:01:56.993 --> 00:01:57.394
a suit.

25
00:01:58.134 --> 00:02:01.396
He lived with his devoted brother Theo who was an art dealer there.

26
00:02:02.856 --> 00:02:04.558
He helped Vincent meet other artists.

27
00:02:05.499 --> 00:02:08.441
In Paris Vincent met a group of artists called the Impressionists.

28
00:02:09.282 --> 00:02:15.367
The Impressionists didn't paint things realistically, but instead they tried to portray emotions through the use of short

29
00:02:15.427 --> 00:02:17.049
brushstrokes and brilliant colors.

30
00:02:17.950 --> 00:02:19.171
Vincent was inspired.

31
00:02:19.791 --> 00:02:24.235
He painted Bridges in Asnieres with bright colors, in the style of the Impressionists.

32
00:02:25.777 --> 00:02:29.360
After two years in Paris, van Gogh longed for the countryside.

33
00:02:30.164 --> 00:02:33.825
He moved from Paris to a small village called Arles in southern France.

34
00:02:34.625 --> 00:02:36.466
He made a bright yellow house his home.

35
00:02:37.286 --> 00:02:42.427
Van Gogh spent his days painting the nearby wheat fields in the summer sun, the local people, and

36
00:02:42.467 --> 00:02:43.628
his beloved yellow house.

37
00:02:45.968 --> 00:02:48.049
Yellow had become van Gogh's favorite color.

38
00:02:48.889 --> 00:02:53.010
It represented all the hope, light, and happiness that he was searching for in life.

39
00:02:53.871 --> 00:02:58.372
He painted fast, as if trying to capture a brief moment or feeling with his paintbrush.

40
00:02:59.208 --> 00:03:03.011
He painted flowers, plum orchards, and cherry blossoms before they faded.

41
00:03:03.832 --> 00:03:06.054
At Arles, he reached his artistic peak.

42
00:03:07.635 --> 00:03:11.499
Around this time van Gogh became fascinated with painting sunflowers.

43
00:03:12.379 --> 00:03:15.202
For him, they represented the energy and warmth of the sun.

44
00:03:16.042 --> 00:03:19.966
He painted many versions of them, in different places and in different shades of yellow.

45
00:03:20.706 --> 00:03:25.610
Today Sunflowers is one of the most famous paintings in the world, and it sold for $39.9 million.

46
00:03:28.816 --> 00:03:32.377
It hangs behind bulletproof glass at a Japanese insurance company.

47
00:03:33.297 --> 00:03:34.718
Vincent was lonely in Arles.

48
00:03:35.638 --> 00:03:37.859
His only friend was the local postman, Roulin.

49
00:03:38.719 --> 00:03:43.060
Vincent painted eight portraits of the postman, as well as portraits of his wife and kids.

50
00:03:43.960 --> 00:03:49.662
Despite his poverty, Roulin refused to be paid for letting Vincent paint him, and he often invited Vincent

51
00:03:49.682 --> 00:03:50.842
for dinner with his family.

52
00:03:52.202 --> 00:03:56.864
Spending time with the Roulins made Vincent feel part of a family, something he had thought he would

53
00:03:56.924 --> 00:03:57.764
never feel again.

54
00:03:58.736 --> 00:04:02.399
Van Gogh had only one friend in his village, and there were no other artists.

55
00:04:03.239 --> 00:04:08.143
So he soon invited his friend, and fellow artist from Paris, Paul Gauguin, to come and work with

56
00:04:08.183 --> 00:04:08.783
him in Arles.

57
00:04:09.704 --> 00:04:12.125
At first the two friends enjoyed each other's company.

58
00:04:13.566 --> 00:04:18.990
They made grand plans for the future and complimented and supported each other's work, but as time passed

59
00:04:19.050 --> 00:04:22.072
by, they started quarreling over their ideas about art.

60
00:04:22.913 --> 00:04:26.956
It was after one big fight with Gauguin that Vincent cut off part of his ear.

61
00:04:27.796 --> 00:04:29.438
He had to be taken to the hospital.

62
00:04:30.198 --> 00:04:31.279
Gauguin left Arles.

63
00:04:33.421 --> 00:04:38.625
Van Gogh painted Self Portrait with a Bandaged Ear soon after, and it shows how miserable and sick

64
00:04:38.665 --> 00:04:39.125
he was.

65
00:04:39.906 --> 00:04:43.609
From this time until his death, he would suffer many mental breakdowns.

66
00:04:44.490 --> 00:04:47.312
Wheat Fields with Crows is one of Vincent's last paintings.

67
00:04:48.193 --> 00:04:49.914
It shows how gloomy his thoughts were.

68
00:04:51.055 --> 00:04:55.839
The sky is dark, the crows appear to be flying madly toward the viewer, and the road seems

69
00:04:55.899 --> 00:04:56.700
to lead nowhere.

70
00:04:57.596 --> 00:05:02.517
Vincent, who was usually optimistic and tried to celebrate life in his paintings, had lost hope.

71
00:05:03.258 --> 00:05:04.778
His illness had overtaken him.

72
00:05:05.638 --> 00:05:08.299
Theo came to see him from Paris, but it was too late.

73
00:05:11.420 --> 00:05:16.121
He died in his brother's arms on July 29, 1890, at the age of 37.

74
00:05:16.881 --> 00:05:21.542
He didn't become an artist until later in life and didn't live long, but in the short time

75
00:05:21.582 --> 00:05:26.744
he painted, Vincent van Gogh created some of the most astonishing and important works of art of all

76
00:05:26.804 --> 00:05:27.144
time.
